@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] editor-focused-native-package
The standalone `default.nix` check MUST execute the source-built editor and broker
under a personal Linux UID over trusted HTTPS. Its local account authorizer and
TLS relay are fixture adapters; passing that standalone check MUST NOT be claimed
as Marshall/Cedar/Audi or Firecracker image acceptance.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] editor-fleet-real-chain
The `fleet.py` and `guest.exs` acceptance scripts MUST exercise real Marshall,
Audi and Lilly releases and actual Firecracker execution of the selected guest
image. Their driver build or type check MUST NOT establish native acceptance;
passing execution MUST identify the tested NixOS, Ubuntu, Arch Linux or AlmaLinux
guest family. Each selected family MUST preserve the same current boot, personal
account, editor policy, file, terminal, recovery and authorization assertions.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification;security] editor-local-browser-inputs
Browser assets, workspace files and gallery responses MUST come from local
bounded fixtures. No public service or production credential may enter this test.
